after endless debates about ownership  nigeria finally got back what was stolen  more than a century ago the first two  bronzes of more than one thousand taken  from the former kingdom of benin  including one showing the head of the  king were handed over at a ceremony at  the german foreign ministry and will  soon be on their way back home  this is a story of european colonialism  we should not forget that germany played  an active role  in this chapter of history  today  more than  120 years later  we state clearly  the head of a king  belongs to the people of nigeria the  thousands of artwork stolen from the  kingdom became a symbol of colonial  injustice when british soldiers looted  the palace in 1897 benin was one of the  most powerful kingdoms on the african  continent  for decades the great great  granddaughter of the king had campaigned  for their return  as a member of the royal family i really  feel very happy that this is happening  it's restoring  dignity and pride  in the culture that i was raised in sad  that is coming  several decades after  but i think that it's important that  that historical injustice is addressed  at this time yeah while germany did not  load the art directly more than a  thousand pieces were bought after being  taken by the british on display until  recently in museums all over the country  while the ownership of the bedin bronzes  has now finally be handed over the  german public will still be able to see  some of them at an exhibition here at  the humble forum soon germany will  continue to take care of the artworks  and will only physically return them at  the request of  nigeria while other european countries  have returned some looted artifacts to  african nations this handover by germany  to nigeria is the largest so far other  countries in the world  will  actually take a cue from germany because  it's a matter of time  they will have to return all student  artifacts to their place of origin  nigeria is building a museum to house  the returning benin bronzes so nigerians  finally do not have to travel to europe  to admire and study their own history  step faster al jazeera in berlin
 

